<figure class="diagram">
  <svg viewBox="0 0 758 236" role="img" aria-label="Two versions of the same fertiliser picker compared. The office version lists products by name and chemical grade as text rows. The shipped version shows a photograph of each sack, because that is how farmers identify what they buy.">
    <defs>
      <marker id="ih" viewBox="0 0 10 10" refX="9" refY="5" markerWidth="7" markerHeight="7" orient="auto-start-reverse">
        <path d="M 0 1 L 9 5 L 0 9 z" fill="currentColor"></path>
      </marker>
    </defs>

    <text x="0" y="12" class="dlabel" fill="currentColor" opacity=".65">What we wrote in the office</text>
    <g class="d-step" style="--i:0">
      <rect x="0" y="24" width="300" height="118" rx="8" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1"></rect>
      <line x1="0" y1="60" x2="300" y2="60" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1" opacity=".3"></line>
      <line x1="0" y1="92" x2="300" y2="92" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1" opacity=".3"></line>
      <text x="16" y="47" font-size="12" fill="currentColor">Urea</text>
      <text x="284" y="47" font-size="11" text-anchor="end" fill="currentColor" opacity=".6">46-0-0</text>
      <text x="16" y="80" font-size="12" fill="currentColor">DAP</text>
      <text x="284" y="80" font-size="11" text-anchor="end" fill="currentColor" opacity=".6">18-46-0</text>
      <text x="16" y="113" font-size="12" fill="currentColor">SOP</text>
      <text x="284" y="113" font-size="11" text-anchor="end" fill="currentColor" opacity=".6">0-0-50</text>
    </g>
    <text x="0" y="166" font-size="11.5" fill="currentColor" opacity=".7">correct, and unreadable to a buyer who has never</text>
    <text x="0" y="182" font-size="11.5" fill="currentColor" opacity=".7">once bought a sack by its chemical grade</text>

    <line class="d-flow" x1="326" y1="83" x2="376" y2="83" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.4" marker-end="url(#ih)"></line>
    <text x="351" y="72" font-size="10.5" text-anchor="middle" fill="currentColor" opacity=".6">ride-along</text>

    <text x="404" y="12" class="dlabel" fill="var(--lapis)">What the farmer asked for</text>
    <g class="d-step" style="--i:1">
      <rect x="404" y="24" width="354" height="118" rx="8" fill="none" stroke="var(--lapis)" stroke-width="1.4"></rect>

      <rect x="426" y="44" width="74" height="78" rx="7" fill="var(--lapis)" opacity=".10"></rect>
      <path d="M 438 56 h 50 v 46 h -50 z" fill="none" stroke="var(--lapis)" stroke-width="1.2"></path>
      <rect x="438" y="70" width="50" height="11" fill="var(--lapis)" opacity=".55"></rect>
      <text x="463" y="116" font-size="11" text-anchor="middle" fill="var(--lapis)">Urea</text>

      <rect x="542" y="44" width="74" height="78" rx="7" fill="var(--lapis)" opacity=".10"></rect>
      <path d="M 554 56 h 50 v 46 h -50 z" fill="none" stroke="var(--lapis)" stroke-width="1.2"></path>
      <circle cx="579" cy="79" r="10" fill="var(--lapis)" opacity=".55"></circle>
      <text x="579" y="116" font-size="11" text-anchor="middle" fill="var(--lapis)">DAP</text>

      <rect x="658" y="44" width="74" height="78" rx="7" fill="var(--lapis)" opacity=".10"></rect>
      <path d="M 670 56 h 50 v 46 h -50 z" fill="none" stroke="var(--lapis)" stroke-width="1.2"></path>
      <path d="M 670 92 l 25 -22 l 25 22 z" fill="var(--lapis)" opacity=".55"></path>
      <text x="695" y="116" font-size="11" text-anchor="middle" fill="var(--lapis)">SOP</text>
    </g>
    <text x="404" y="166" font-size="11.5" fill="var(--lapis)">a picture of the sack he already recognises on the</text>
    <text x="404" y="182" font-size="11.5" fill="var(--lapis)">shelf — the name is the caption, not the control</text>

    <line x1="0" y1="206" x2="758" y2="206" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1" opacity=".18"></line>
    <text x="0" y="228" font-size="11.5" fill="currentColor" opacity=".7">the requirement did not change. the thing the user taps did.</text>
  </svg>
  <figcaption>
    A farmer asked for pictures of urea and DAP instead of labels. Nothing about the catalogue, the pricing or the order flow was wrong — the identifier was. This is the whole argument for ride-alongs in one screen: the office version is accurate and the field version is usable, and you cannot tell which is which from a desk.
  </figcaption>
</figure>
